Z||000000||batboy||07-11-2000||09:23 PM||||No, I didn't get get to play snugglebunnies with a hot babe...LOL. I'm not that lucky! I've been checking out a red 88 GT that's been sitting at a small auto repair shop for the last few weeks. I stopped in today to find out the story on it. Turns out it's a customer's car and it's not for sale.<P>Now here's the lucky part. The shop owner/mechanic told me he's fixing cracked manifolds on it and has done this with several V6 Fieros in the past. I told him as soon as I fix my clutch problems on my 85 GT, I'd bring it to him to do my manifold too. He told me, sure thing, he needs the business.<P>The other guy who was at the shop too (the shop owner's brother-in-law) asked me a few questions about the Batmobile (which is what I pulled up in). Told me it looked good lowered and asked what I had in it, because it didn't sound stock. I told him it had a V8, and he didn't even act surprised. Then he told me he used to work at a big body/restoration shop that did a lot of Fiero based kit cars and a few of them they installed V8's in.<P>We wandered outside to look at my car. I mentioned I'd like to get it painted sometime before next fall. He told me that he had his own body shop just two miles away and that he'd painted several Fieros in the past. So, I asked for an estimate.<P>We discussed a two-tone paint job and he suggested a few simple, but excellent graphics to help set it off. He also told me that several of his customers had won car show awards and offered to give me references to check them out. He finally said he could paint it they way we discussed and fix the couple little boo-boos for $650 (base coat/clear coat), which included a 5-year guarantee.<P>When I got home, I looked him up in the phone book and sure enough he's listed under body shops. So, I might have to check out his references. I loved his ideas about setting the car off and making it a one-of-a-kind custom paint job. The Batmobile is worth it.<P>Wow, I finally found a couple people fairly close by that aren't afraid to tackle Fiero jobs...and they both claim to have lots of Fiero experience. Life is good.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 07-11-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||Patrick||07-12-2000||01:12 AM||||<BR>Maybe they've got sisters...||||reg||12
